From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 12:07:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/46] game: drop the last `register` (no codegen change)

Same rationale as the engine/ and goddard/ patches: the keyword is a no-op
for modern compilers and removed in C++17; nothing here takes the address
of the variable. Verified byte-identical assembly before and after.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/game/object_helpers.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/game/object_helpers.c b/src/game/object_helpers.c
index c6626e54..8df2765b 100644
--- a/src/game/object_helpers.c
+++ b/src/game/object_helpers.c
@@ -2403,7 +2403,7 @@ void bhv_init_room(void) {
 }
 
 void cur_obj_enable_rendering_if_mario_in_room(void) {
-    register s32 marioInRoom;
+    s32 marioInRoom;
 
     if (o->oRoom != -1 && gMarioCurrentRoom != 0) {
         if (gMarioCurrentRoom == o->oRoom) {
